<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bokmål</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bokmål is the more widely used of the two official written standards of Norwegian, alongside Nynorsk. It descends from the Danish written language used in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> during the union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, adapted to Norwegian speech through spelling reforms from 1907, and received its present name in 1929. It is used by most Norwegians.</p></div>
